      },
      "source": [
        "### Data dictionary\n",
        "\n",
        "| Column | Meaning |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| `Age` | Age at diagnosis (years) |\n",
        "| `Race` | Ethnicity (SEER categories: White / Black / Other) |\n",
        "| `Marital Status` | Marital status at diagnosis |\n",
        "| `T Stage` | Extent of the primary tumor (AJCC), T1 (small) → T4 (extensive) |\n",
        "| `N Stage` | Regional lymph node involvement, N1 → N3 (increasing) |\n",
        "| `6th Stage` | Overall AJCC 6th edition stage (combines T, N, and metastatic status) |\n",
        "| `Grade` | Histologic differentiation grade of the tumor (I = well differentiated → IV = anaplastic) |\n",
        "| `A Stage` | Regional (localized/loco-regional) vs Distant (metastatic) |\n",
        "| `Tumor Size` | Tumor diameter (mm) |\n",
        "| `Estrogen Status` / `Progesterone Status` | Hormone receptor status (Positive/Negative) |\n",
        "| `Regional Node Examined` | No. of lymph nodes surgically examined |\n",
        "| `Reginol Node Positive` | No. of lymph nodes found positive (with metastasis) |\n",
        "| `Survival Months` | Months of observed follow-up |\n",
        "| `Status` | Status at the end of follow-up: Alive (alive/censored) or Dead (deceased) |\n",
        "\n",
        "`Survival Months` and `Status` are **only** used to build the label — they are not legitimate model features (using them would be data leakage: they would use the very outcome you're trying to predict)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d7d680b2",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d7d680b2"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Label creation — 5-year Overall Survival\n",
        "\n",
        "The task is: **predict whether a patient will have died within 5 years (60 months) of diagnosis**, using only clinico-pathological information available at diagnosis/initial staging.\n",
        "\n",
        "Not all patients can be used: anyone still \"Alive\" with a shorter follow-up than 60 months is still under observation — their 5-year outcome is not known (censoring), and they must be excluded rather than forced into one of the two classes.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **label = 1** (death within 5 years): `Status == \"Dead\"` and `Survival Months < 60`\n",
        "- **label = 0** (survives to 5 years): `Survival Months >= 60` (regardless of what happens afterwards)\n",
        "- **excluded**: `Status == \"Alive\"` and `Survival Months < 60` (unknown outcome)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 14,
      "id": "39f463e7",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.286548Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.286498Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.290141Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.289971Z"
        },
        "id": "39f463e7",
        "outputId": "b9d94d65-79fe-4294-addb-79c220ba6153"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Evaluable patients: 3270  |  excluded (censored before 5 years): 753 (18.7% of the original cohort)\n",
            "label\n",
            "0    0.863\n",
            "1    0.137\n",
            "Name: share, dtype: float64\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "HORIZON = 60  # months\n",
        "\n",
        "survived = df[df[\"Survival Months\"] >= HORIZON].copy()\n",
        "survived[\"label\"] = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "died_early = df[(df[\"Status\"] == \"Dead\") & (df[\"Survival Months\"] < HORIZON)].copy()\n",
        "died_early[\"label\"] = 1\n",
        "\n",
        "excluded = df[(df[\"Status\"] == \"Alive\") & (df[\"Survival Months\"] < HORIZON)]\n",
        "\n",
        "task_df = pd.concat([survived, died_early], ignore_index=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Evaluable patients: {len(task_df)}  |  excluded (censored before 5 years): {len(excluded)} \"\n",
        "      f\"({len(excluded)/len(df)*100:.1f}% of the original cohort)\")\n",
        "print(task_df[\"label\"].value_counts(normalize=True).rename(\"share\").round(3))"
      ]
    },
    {
