      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Train/test split and Cross-Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "Stratified split (keeps the same proportion of events in train and test) with a fixed seed, so all groups start from the same data.\n",
        "\n",
        "The columns `Survival Months`, `Status` (used to build the label) and the `label` itself are separated out from `X`. **`6th Stage` is not removed here**: it's one of the questions you should ask yourselves during EDA and feature engineering (hint: check its relationship with `T Stage`/`N Stage`/`A Stage`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 15,
      "id": "e39612a9",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.291081Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.291025Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.882632Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.882401Z"
        },
        "id": "e39612a9",
        "outputId": "4176118b-0777-4825-889b-eaafdb1a3def"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Train: (2452, 13)  Test: (818, 13)\n",
            "Event prevalence (label=1) — train: 0.137  test: 0.137\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, StratifiedKFold\n",
        "\n",
        "LEAKAGE_COLS = [\"Survival Months\", \"Status\", \"label\"]  # do NOT use as a feature\n",
        "\n",
        "X = task_df.drop(columns=LEAKAGE_COLS)\n",
        "y = task_df[\"label\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X, y, test_size=0.25, stratify=y, random_state=SEED\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Train:\", X_train.shape, \" Test:\", X_test.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Event prevalence (label=1) — train:\", round(y_train.mean(), 3), \" test:\", round(y_test.mean(), 3))"
      ]
    },
