      "source": [
        "## 4. Data pre-processing\n",
        "\n",
        "We define a common preprocessor (scaling of numeric variables + one-hot encoding of categoricals), to be used as the first step of any scikit-learn `Pipeline` you build. It must **always be fit on the train set only** (inside CV or on the final train set) and never on the whole dataset, to avoid data leakage between train and test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 17,
      "id": "b46e630e",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.885822Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.885761Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.931292Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-23T15:30:32.931011Z"
        },
        "id": "b46e630e"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
        "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\n",
        "\n",
        "NUM_COLS = [\"Age\", \"Tumor Size\", \"Regional Node Examined\", \"Reginol Node Positive\"]\n",
        "CAT_COLS = [\"Race\", \"Marital Status\", \"T Stage\", \"N Stage\", \"6th Stage\",\n",
        "            \"Grade\", \"A Stage\", \"Estrogen Status\", \"Progesterone Status\"]\n",
        "assert set(NUM_COLS) | set(CAT_COLS) == set(X.columns)\n",
        "\n",
        "def make_preprocessor():\n",
        "    return ColumnTransformer([\n",
        "        (\"num\", StandardScaler(), NUM_COLS),\n",
        "        (\"cat\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\"), CAT_COLS),\n",
